using System.Collections.Generic;

namespace TerraKnight.Items
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Every combat weapon's damage, after Terraria's own strengths (the user's 2026-10-28 "做武器的伤害平衡吧，另外其他三职业的伤害是应该
    /// 比战士高的，因为战士防御高" and "可以参考一下原版武器的伤害"). Every weapon was used six seconds on Dirtmouth's Target Dummy (suite
    /// classdps, TK_CLASSDPS_ALL=1; Master, the median defense of the stage's bosses, the stage's reference kit) twice:
    /// in a world of Terraria's weapons, which gives its Terraria strength (that measurement at its Terraria damage,
    /// defense aside), and in a world of the remade weapons, which gives what it does now. Within a stage and class the
    /// weapons stand as in Terraria: each one's strength over the best's, ^0.6, at least 0.35; the best meets the
    /// class's target, a share of the stage's figure (85, 115, 190, 340, 620, 1500 a second): the warrior 0.87 of it,
    /// the ranger, the mage and the summoner 1.04 (1.2 times the warrior, who has the most defense; the four together
    /// as before). A summoner's target is its minions' and its whip's together: the whip a quarter, the same at every
    /// stage. Each damage is solved from the remade measurements, within 0.3 to 3 times the last; then the table was
    /// measured again three times, and each time the weapons more than 15% off their target (the mean of the runs at
    /// their damage) were solved again on a line through all their measurements (a hit's damage goes with the
    /// weapon's), down to 0.2 times. A summoner's staff whose minions with the stage's best whip would go over the
    /// target by 15% is brought down to it, and one raised toward its own target stops there: the whip's tag adds to
    /// every minion hit, most to the fast hitters (the Cattiva). Weapons the dummy can't measure (rains and streams, or
    /// under 15% of their group's best) take Terraria's damage times their group's median factor, brought down to their
    /// group's best when a measurement found them over it. The mod's own weapons stand by the weapons they were made
    /// beside (the Vengeful Spirit's and the Shade Soul's by the Terraria weapons in SoulWave.Balance and
    /// Shade.Balance, the Abyss Shriek's high in stage 4, the others in the middle of their group), raised at most
    /// twice. The True Copper Shortsword does what the Zenith does a second (its own sword hits harder, so its damage
    /// is lower). The values are the last word on these weapons: the recipe upgrades, the timber cap, the native floor
    /// and LateWeaponCalibration leave them be. Written by scratchpad calib_ref.py (the two classdps runs,
    /// itemdump.json), calib_pass2.py (the verification runs) and write_calib_vanilla.py.
    /// </summary>
